  "explanation": "While adults of all ages can contract COVID-19, the risk of becoming seriously ill is not uniform across age groups. Data from China indicate that severe outcomes and fatalities are predominantly observed in older adults, particularly those aged 60 years and above, with approximately 80% of deaths occurring in this age group and only one death recorded in individuals aged 19 years or younger [1]. Similarly, United States data show that 80% of COVID-19 fatalities occurred among individuals aged 65 years and older, with no recorded ICU admissions or deaths among those aged 19 years or younger [1]. These findings demonstrate that older adults, especially those with pre-existing health conditions, are at significantly higher risk of severe illness and mortality from COVID-19, whereas younger adults and children are much less likely to experience severe or fatal outcomes [1]."
}

